ight),$ we need to find the slope of the tangent to $f(x)$ at $x=\\dfrac32.$\n\nLet's consider the graph of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in [1,2].$ Notice that $x=\\dfrac32$ lies in this interval.\n\n![](images/90/9067715198a510cc1399bb257352babb1ac093db1c80c611c2236c10b43607bc.png)\n\nThe slope of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in(1,2)$ is constant and equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{Δf}{Δx} & =\\frac{0-2}{2-1}=\\frac{-2}{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f'\\left(\\dfrac32\\right)=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096376 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096376 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6a/6ae60cb8606fb75aa49251ad894ce6a56173d6d5310aba0018e6c6933d1b93fe.png)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y = f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ are given above. Find $h'(-1)$ where $h(x)=f(x)+g(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096376 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9811f16e-75aa-5982-b97b-cc59b33fb7d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096376 #edb/ref 1074 "The addition rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\nh'(x) = f'(x) + g'(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\nh'(-1) =f'(-1) + g'(-1).\n$$\n\nAlso, notice that $x=-1$ corresponds to \n\n- the interval $x\\in(-2,1)$ for the function $f,$ and\n\n- the interval $x\\in(-2,0)$ for the function $g,$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/1c/1c6ff6240abc7b56f058547e29ef250514fd19723057a65089ef0fa6da0ec044.png)\n\n- The slope of $y=f(x)$ is constant on $x\\in(-2,1)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\Delta f}{\\Delta x} = \\dfrac{1-(-1)}{1-(-2)} = \\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f'(-1)=\\dfrac{2}{3}.$\n\n- The slope of $y=g(x)$ is constant on $x\\in(-2,0)$ and equals\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\Delta g}{\\Delta x} = \\dfrac{-1-2}{0-(-2)} = -\\dfrac{3}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g'(-1)=-\\dfrac{3}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(-1) & ={f}^{′}(-1)+{g}^{′}(-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096377 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10891" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096377 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/69/69dd5f35d420746ebecc4fc7b01f09f0be01ccbc9b02cc3987533be5c0ec58ad.png)\n\nThe graphs of the functions $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ are given above. Find $h'(0)$ where $h(x)=f(x)g(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096377 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1fb2491b-f442-57e3-990f-65bf1270d847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096377 #edb/ref 1074 "The product rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\nh'(x) = f'(x)\\cdot g(x)+f(x)\\cdot g'(x).\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\nh'(0)=f'(0)\\cdot g(0)+f(0)\\cdot g'(0).\n$$\n\nFrom the graphs above, we obtain that $f(0)=1$ and $g(0)=-1.$ \n\nAdditionally,\n\n- The slope of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in(-1,1)$ equals $-1.$ So, $f'(0)=-1.$\n\n- The slope of $y=g(x)$ on $x\\in(-0.5,1)$ equals $2.$ So, $g'(0)=2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(0) & ={f}^{′}(0)\\cdot g(0)+f(0)\\cdot {g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096378 #edb/ref 1069 "e-10892" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096378 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/9c/9cd56facb5599cc8f2ffd8de8ee152cfec47844fc96d3daddb42e59afb0c8a57.png)\n\nGiven the plots of $y=f(x)$ and $y=g(x)$ above, find $h'(2)$ where $h(x)=\\dfrac{f(x)}{g(x)}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096378 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e929c25-68b1-5a6b-92a0-d12b90a112e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096378 #edb/ref 1074 "The quotient rule for derivatives gives\n\n$$\nh'(x) = \\dfrac{f'(x)\\cdot g(x)-f(x)\\cdot g'(x)}{(g(x))^2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n$$\nh'(2) = \\dfrac{f'(2)\\cdot g(2)-f(2)\\cdot g'(2)}{(g(2))^2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph above, we obtain that $f(2)=1$ and $g(2)=0.5.$\n\nAdditionally:\n\n- The slope of $y=f(x)$ on $x\\in(1,3)$ equals $-1.$ So, $f'(2)=-1.$\n\n- The slope of $y=g(x)$ on $x\\in(1,3)$ equals $-0.5.$ So, $g'(2)=-0.5.$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{′}(2) & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(2)\\cdot g(2)-f(2)\\cdot {g}^{′}(2)}{{(g(2))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (0.5)-(1)\\cdot (-0.5)}{(0.5)^{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050711 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050961 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186241071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317545 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186317546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186341896 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186573874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Derivative of a Function From Its Graph" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096804 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0a16e7b6-2a09-5aeb-9a8b-ea8fb1d59807" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096805 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096805 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096805 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096805 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096805 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096805 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186240937 #edb/ref